  "goodToKnow": "Der Löwenzahn is the dandelion, named for its jagged leaves like a lion's teeth (as in French dent-de-lion). Its fluffy seed head is die Pusteblume (blow flower). Young leaves are eaten in salads, and rabbits love them. Löwenzahn is also a long-running ZDF children's science show, first hosted by Peter Lustig from 1981. Its plural is rare."
